Chapter: InductionList

 Stage 5: structural induction with a BINARY constructor. `append xs Nil
 === xs` over a user-defined list. The MyCons case reduces to
 `MyCons h (append t MyNil) === MyCons h t`, discharged by `cong ih` where
 ih is `append t MyNil === t`. Here `cong` must solve its function
 variable to `MyCons h` -- a PARTIAL application of a 2-argument
 constructor -- which the unifier handles by peeling the saturated
 constructor `MyCons h X` as a curried type application
 `(MyCons h) X`. add-zero only needed unary `Succ`; this needs the N-ary
 peel.

Section: List

  MyList =
   | MyNil
   | MyCons (Integer) (MyList)

  append : MyList, MyList -> MyList
  append (xs) (ys) = when xs
   is MyNil -> ys
   is MyCons (h) (t) -> MyCons h (append t ys)

Section: Proof

  claim append-nil : for all (xs : MyList), append xs MyNil === xs
  proof append-nil =
   induction on xs
    is MyNil -> Refl
    is MyCons (h) (t) (ih) -> cong ih
   qed

Section: Main

  opening : [Console] Nothing
  opening = act
   print-line-uni "induction-list ok"
  end
